<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Shared reactor core glow mote. Attached per-pawn by ReactorGlowMote.Maintain
    from each reactor hediff's Tick (not TickInterval — see Hediff_VanometricReactor
    for the offscreen-throttling rationale). One mote def serves all reactor
    variants; per-reactor colour is supplied via Mote.instanceColor in code.

    altitudeLayer=Darkness puts this above the unnatural-darkness section-layer
    mesh (same trick CompNoctolEyes uses for noctol eye glow). In normal
    lighting it just renders as an additive overlay above the pawn at the same
    visual position as the chest body attachment.

    drawSize=0.55 is empirically tuned to match the chest core on a reference
    pawn. Pure canvas-ratio math (chest 0.2 × 256/128 = 0.4) undershoots here
    because PawnRenderNodeWorker_AttachmentBody composes additional scale
    factors beyond bodyGraphicScale (chest-specific drawData scale, root pawn
    graphic scale, etc.) that the mote rendering path doesn't replicate. The
    RenderNodeSafe mode does go through AttachmentBody and so uses the
    canvas-ratio 0.4 directly — see HediffDefs_VanometricReactor.xml. Tune by
    eye against the chest core if you swap textures. ReactorGlowMote.Maintain
    multiplies by the pawn's bodyGraphicScale average so the glow still tracks
    body-type variation (Thin/Fat/Hulk).

    solidTime=600 (10s) is well beyond the 1-tick maintenance cadence; the
    Maintain() call in the hediff tick path keeps the mote indefinitely alive.

    Graphic_Mote (not Graphic_Single) is load-bearing: Graphic_Single inherits
    Graphic.DrawWorker which never reads Mote.instanceColor. Graphic_Mote
    overrides DrawWorker to push instanceColor (including alpha) into a
    material property block, which is how per-reactor colour tinting and
    south-only alpha gating actually reach the shader. Picking the wrong
    class here makes both the per-reactor tint and the visibility-by-facing
    behaviour silently no-op.

    renderQueue=4000 sits in Unity's transparent queue, ahead of the darkness
    overlay's mesh queue so the glow draws over it.
  -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="MoteBase">
    <defName>Mote_AAHReactorGlow</defName>
    <thingClass>ArchotechAndroidHardware.Mote_ReactorGlow</thingClass>
    <altitudeLayer>Darkness</altitudeLayer>
    <mote>
      <needsMaintenance>True</needsMaintenance>
      <solidTime>600</solidTime>
    </mote>
    <graphicData>
      <renderQueue>4000</renderQueue>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Mote</graphicClass>
      <shaderType>MoteGlow</shaderType>
      <texPath>Things/Mote/AAHReactorGlow</texPath>
      <drawSize>(0.55, 0.55)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>